  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\nWe would like to ask you if you are willing to participate in our research
    project. Your participation is voluntary. Please read the text below carefully
    and ask the conducting person about anything you do not understand or would like
    to know.\r\n\r\nWhat is investigated and how?\r\n\r\nThis study investigates
    how the spatial layout of an Emergency Department (ED) affects team communication,
    collaboration, and care coordination. Participants will take part in simulated
    emergency scenarios within a online interactive 3D simulation environment, featuring
    different architectural configurations (cockpit variations). \r\n\r\nData will
    be collected through the online environment (tracking positions and movement
    trajectories), audio and video recordings of the collaborative sessions, as well
    as questionnaires and brief debriefings. The results aim to help design safer
    and more efficient ED environments. \r\n\r\nWho can participate?\r\n\r\nParticipants
    include university students and volunteers participating in simulated healthcare
    scenarios, including those taking on patient roles. All participants are involved
    in collaborative tasks and provide feedback relevant to the study objectives.\r\n\r\nInclusion
    Criteria\r\nYou may participate if you:\r\n    \u2022 Are 18 years old or above\r\n   
    \u2022 Have sufficient English proficiency to understand the study instructions
    and consent information\r\n    \u2022 Are able to use basic computer.\r\n\r\nExclusion
    criteria:\r\n    \u2022 Experience severe motion sickness or strong discomfort
    while interacting with screen-based or 3D visual content \r\n    \u2022 Are unable
    to comfortably use computer/online interface for the duration of the experiment
    \r\n    \u2022 Individuals unwilling to be audio and video recorded for research
    purposes.\r\n    \u2022 Individuals unable or unwilling to follow instructions
    for the simulation scenarios.\r\n\r\nWhat am I supposed to do as a participant?\r\nIf
    you agree to participate, you will take part in one experimental session lasting
    approximately 30 to 45 minutes. \r\n\r\nYou will:\r\n    \u2022 Receive an introduction
    to the study procedures\r\n    \u2022 Complete a short training session to learn
    how to use the online interface.\r\n    \u2022 Participate in three simulated
    teamwork sessions under different layout conditions\r\n    \u2022 Communicate
    and collaborate with other participants to complete assigned tasks\r\n    \u2022
    Complete short questionnaires after the tasks\r\n    \u2022 Take part in a short
    debriefing at the end of the session\r\nYou may take breaks if needed and may
    stop participating at any time without giving a reason.\r\nWhat are my rights
    during participation?  \r\nYour participation in this study is voluntary. You
    can withdraw your participation at any time without giving reasons and without
    any disadvantage.\r\n\r\nWhat risks and benefits can I expect?\r\nThe study involves\_minimal
    risk. You may experience mild fatigue, temporary discomfort from prolonged screen
    exposure or interaction with 3D visual content , or mild stress during the simulations.
    You can take breaks, request adjustments, ask questions, or stop participating
    at any time.\r\nYour data will be\_pseudonymised and securely stored, and no
    identifying information will be shared or published. Video and sensor data will
    be used only for research purposes.\r\nThere are\_no direct personal benefits\_from
    taking part. However, the results may help improve the design of healthcare environments
    and support safer, more effective teamwork in emergency care settings.\r\nWill
    I be compensated for my participation?\r\nYes. All participants will be recruited
    specifically for the study and be compensated with an hourly wage in accordance
    with ETH student helper guidelines and aligned with fair market rates. The timing
    and delivery method are communicated to participants in advance. \r\nCompensation
    is provided\_independently of study performance\_and will also be granted if
    you choose to withdraw from the study early. Participation is entirely voluntary.\r\nWhat
    data is collected from me and how is it used?\r\nThe following data is collected
    from you:\r\n    \u2022 Identifying data (voice/video recordings)\r\n    \u2022
    Other (research) data (e.g. survey responses)\r\n    \u2022 Action Trajectory
    in Unity\r\n\r\nThis data is collected to understand how spatial layout influences
    communication, collaboration, and care quality during simulated emergency scenarios.\r\n\r\nAll
    participants will be assigned a\_unique participation number that will be linked
    to a non-identifying role label (e.g., nurse 1). Identifying data (e.g., video
    or audio recordings) will be\_stored separately from other research data\_on
    secure, ETH-approved servers. Access to identifying data and the link between
    identities and participation numbers is restricted to the\_principal investigators
    and authorised members of the research team only. Identifying data will be deleted
    or fully anonymised once it is no longer required for analysis.\r\nAll data will
    be\_anonymised as soon as the purpose of the data processing permits. Research
    results will be published in\_scientific journals, conference presentations,
    and reports. Only\_anonymised and aggregated results\_will be published, and
    no conclusions about individual participants will be drawn from any publication.\r\nAnonymised
    data may be published for further use\_(e.g., in a scientific data repository)
    in line with open science practices and institutional guidelines.\r\nNo non-anonymised
    data will be shared with third parties, including industry partners.\r\nWho is
    funding the study?\r\nThis study is funded by the Chair of Cognitive Science
    at ETH Z\xFCrich, led by Prof. Dr. Christoph H\xF6lscher, and by a Swiss National
    Science Foundation (SNF) research grant awarded to Prof. Dr. Christoph H\xF6lscher.\r\n\_\r\nNo
    other funding sources are involved.\r\n\r\nIs any damage to health insured? \r\nDamage
    related to the study is covered by ETH Zurich's public liability insurance (Basler
    Versicherungen, policy no. 30/4.078.362).\r\n\r\nWho reviewed the study?\r\nThis
    study was reviewed and approved by the ETH Zurich Ethics Committee under application
    number XX ETHICS-YYY.\r\n\r\nComplaints office\r\nThe secretariat of the ETH
    Zurich Ethics Committee is available to help you with complaints in connection
    with your participation in the study. Contact: ethics@sl.ethz.ch or 0041 44 632
    85 72.\r\n\r\nConsent Form\r\n\r\nI confirm my consent electronically by selecting
    the agreement option before proceeding:\r\n\r\n    \u2022 I have read and understood
    the study information.\r\n    \u2022 I had enough time to decide about my participation
    and am taking part in the study voluntarily.\r\n    \u2022 I fulfil the stated
    conditions for participation.\r\n    \u2022 I consent that the data described
    above may be collected from me and used as described.\r\n    \u2022 I know that
    the data collected from me may be published in anonymised form.\r\n    \u2022
    I know that I can cancel my participation any time.\r\n\r\nI would like to be
    informed about the results of this study\r\n\r\n\u2610 Yes, name, phone number
    or e-mail: \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\u2610
    No\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nName of participant\r\n\r\n\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\r\n\r\nPlace,
    date\r\nSignature participant\r\n\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\r\n\r\n\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\r\nPlace,
    date\r\nSignature conducting person\r\n\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\r\n\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\r\n\r\n"
